@startuml d3_flattened_fk
!include _style.puml
title D3 — flattened-fk  (the grandparent key copied down to the grandchild)

entity "charity" as c {
  * charity_id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * name : TEXT
  * country : TEXT
  * founded_on : DATE
}
entity "person" as p {
  * person_id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * charity_id : BIGINT <<FK>>
  * full_name : TEXT
  * email : TEXT
  * joined_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
}
entity "donation" as d {
  * donation_id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * person_id : BIGINT <<FK>>
  <back:#FFF3CD>* charity_id : BIGINT <<FK>> — denormalised</back>
  * amount_cents : BIGINT
  * currency : CHAR(3)
  * donated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
  note : TEXT
}
c ||--o{ p
p ||--o{ d
c ||..o{ d : "redundant shortcut\n(derivable via person)"

note bottom of d
  **all D2 indexes, plus**
  **+ donation_charity_time_idx** (charity_id, donated_at DESC)
  **+ donation_charity_amount_idx** (charity_id) INCLUDE (amount_cents)

  charity_id on donation is pure redundancy — it is
  always equal to the donation's person's charity_id.
  Buying with that redundancy:
   * six of twelve queries lose a join
   * "total donated to a charity" becomes an
     index-only scan, never touching the heap

  Paying with it:
   * a wider row and another index to maintain
   * an invariant the database does not enforce.
     Move a person between charities and every
     donation row is now lying.
end note
@enduml
